      }), ". Client generators like OpenAPI Generator can automatically create type-safe clients from API specifications, but only if your parameter design follows conventions. Inconsistent or non-standard parameter patterns create generated clients that are awkward to use, forcing developers to write manual client code instead."]
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.h2, {
      children: "Best Practices and Design Guidelines"
    }), "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
      children: ["Start every API endpoint design by identifying what you're operating on-the resource-and make its identifier a path variable. This grounds your design in REST's resource-oriented model and ensures your URLs form a coherent hierarchy. Whether you're creating, retrieving, updating, or deleting, the resource identifier belongs in the path: ", _jsx(_components.code, {
